From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 20:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] linux 3.10: force gnu89 when building with GCC 15

GCC 15 defaults C compilation to gnu23. In C23, bool, true, and false are
keywords, but this vendor Linux 3.10 tree still defines bool and false in
kernel headers. That makes the build fail before the kernel proper is built.

Force the legacy kernel dialect explicitly so modern toolchains compile the
old kernel source the same way older toolchains did.
---
 Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 0be7e46..c4f89d0 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -379,7 +379,7 @@ KBUILD_CPPFLAGS := -D__KERNEL__
 KBUILD_CFLAGS   := -Wall -Wundef -Wstrict-prototypes -Wno-trigraphs \
 		   -fno-strict-aliasing -fno-common \
 		   -Werror-implicit-function-declaration \
-		   -Wno-format-security \
+		   -Wno-format-security -std=gnu89 \
 		   -fno-delete-null-pointer-checks
 KBUILD_AFLAGS_KERNEL :=
 KBUILD_CFLAGS_KERNEL :=
-- 
